`openCaptureStore()` throws "not implemented" when opening shared captures

I was trying to keep a shared note in my SilverBullet space for later, but opening the capture store fails in `@silverbulletmd/silverbullet`.

This reproduces it from the repository root in a browser context:

```ts
import { openCaptureStore } from "./client/capture/store.ts";
const scriptUrl = "https://notes.example/personal/service_worker.js";
const store = await openCaptureStore(scriptUrl);
await store.configure("writer", true);
await store.stage({ title: "Reading", text: "Keep for later", url: "" }, []);
console.log(await store.list("writer"));
```

Opening the store should let me stage and retrieve shared notes and attachments, including after reopening it. The related storage and sign-out support should also work: memory KV reads and writes should support persistence, browser logout should coordinate saving and cleanup across tabs, and UUID generation should support browsers without the native convenience method. Use the existing doc comments, interfaces and surrounding callers for the expected behaviour.

Instead, the opening call rejects with `Error("not implemented")`. Throwing stubs remain across `client/capture/store.ts`, `client/data/memory_kv_primitives.ts`, `client/logout.ts`, `client/logout_state.ts` and `plug-api/lib/crypto.ts`; fill in those stubs so capture storage and the related sign-out flow work together.

